# Citation metadata for Sarimax.jl. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo's
# GitHub integration reads .zenodo.json for the archived release.
#
# TO CONFIRM BEFORE THE RELEASE (maintainers): the author lists and affiliations of the
# software and of the article (only the package author recorded in Project.toml is listed;
# other contributors in the git history include Davi Michel Valladao, Luisa Millen Compasso
# and Joao Quintella), ORCID identifiers, and the version DOIs of the software and data
# records, which exist only once the Zenodo records are published.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Sarimax.jl, please cite the software and the article below. To cite the exact
  code and data used for the article's results, cite the version DOIs of the archived
  release and of the experimental-artifact record (see replication/ijf-2026/README.md).
title: "Sarimax.jl: optimization-based SARIMAX modeling in Julia"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LAMPSPUC/Sarimax.jl"
url: "https://lampspuc.github.io/Sarimax.jl/dev/"
abstract: >-
  Sarimax.jl estimates SARIMA and SARIMAX models by formulating them as explicit JuMP
  optimization problems: coefficients and residuals are decision variables, the model
  dynamics are constraints, and the objective function, coefficient constraints,
  regularization and solver (local, such as Ipopt, or global, such as SCIP) are
  user-selectable.
keywords:
  - time series
  - forecasting
  - SARIMAX
  - ARIMA
  - mathematical optimization
  - JuMP
  - Julia
authors:
  - family-names: Duarte
    given-names: Luiz Fernando Cunha
    affiliation: "LAMPS, Department of Electrical Engineering, Pontifical Catholic University of Rio de Janeiro (PUC-Rio)"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "SARIMAX.jl: Open-Source Optimization-Based SARIMAX Modeling in Julia"
  journal: "International Journal of Forecasting"
  status: submitted
  notes: "Special issue: Advances in Open Source Forecasting Software"
  authors:
    - family-names: Duarte
      given-names: Luiz Fernando Cunha
